WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.890
With the absurd amount of content flooding
our multiplex screens every year, it stands

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.840
to reason that more than a few films will
fail to score with the public.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.500
As different as they may be, these movies
all suffered the same unfortunate fate.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.000
Some were unnecessary, some struggled to market
themselves and some simply failed to deliver,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.440
but every last one of them tanked at the box
office.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.140
Here’s why.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.860
Solo: A Star Wars Story

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.399
It seems preposterous to even entertain the
notion that a Star Wars movie could be anything

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.360
but a smash hit, but here we are.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:39.140
Solo: A Star Wars Story opened in May to something
of a shrug from audiences.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.140
It's not even that the movie was particularly
bad, it's just that Solo never seemed to be

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.720
a movie that Star Wars fans ever wanted.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.180
Many fans felt that fleshing out the backstory
of one of the franchise's most beloved characters

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.860
was completely unnecessary.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:59.220
And while Donald Glover shone as a young Lando
Calrissian and Alden Ehrenreich turned in

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.800
an admirable performance as Solo himself,
these characters were afflicted by a thin

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.900
story which added little to the saga as a
whole.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:12.679
Releasing Solo five months after The Last
Jedi, and only a month after Avengers: Infinity

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.580
War, can’t have helped things, either.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.240
Skyscraper

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:22.140
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson’s latest summer
blockbuster seemed almost genetically engineered

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:22.920
for success.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:28.540
It was a fresh IP, hyped as this generation’s
Die Hard, and starred one of the most bankable

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.360
stars working in Hollywood today.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.299
But while critics were split down the middle
when Skyscraper hit theaters, audiences found

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.540
themselves supremely uninterested by the movie’s
release.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:44.959
With a $125 million budget and a gargantuan
advertising campaign to match, Skyscraper

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.640
would have had to do absolute gangbusters
at the box office to avoid losing money.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.279
Despite a decent overseas reception, thanks
largely to the movie’s Hong Kong setting

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.540
and diverse cast, success just never materialized.

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:03.020
The movie’s derivative plot probably frustrated
audiences as much as it did critics, and,

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:08.700
with Skyscraper coming so soon after the release
of Jumanji and Rampage, you can’t discount

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.540
Rock fatigue as a factor in the movie’s
unfortunate demise.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.320
A Wrinkle in Time

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:21.000
Disney’s adaptation of the beloved novel
by Madeleine L’Engle encouraged high expectations.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:27.040
It had a stellar cast and an admirable commitment
to diversity, being the first big-budget,

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.520
tentpole movie to be directed by a black woman,
the exceedingly talented Ava DuVernay.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.380
With Young Adult franchises like Harry Potter
and The Hunger Games dominating the box office

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.200
in recent years, A Wrinkle in Time could reasonably
have been expected to be a smash hit.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.780
Sadly, this never happened.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.520
The movie failed to encourage the kind of
diverse audiences Black Panther had gathered

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:53.450
a few weeks earlier and, perhaps due to its
lukewarm critical response, none of the usual

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.840
young adult movie crowds showed up, either.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:01.280
The film's convoluted marketing campaign didn't
help, and Wrinkle ended up scraping together

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.640
just over $100 million in the United States.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:10.480
“To you I give the gift of your faults…
you’re welcome.”

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.560
The Hurricane Heist

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:18.300
The involvement of Rob Cohen, best known for
directing the original Fast and the Furious

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:23.850
and xXx , lent a degree of anticipation to
The Hurricane Heist’s box office chances,

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.370
and the more optimistic dared to hope the
movie might have been one of those high-octane,

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:33.240
stunt-heavy action flicks which inevitably
bloom into profitable franchises.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.420
Unfortunately, critics skewered the movie
at release for its rip-off narrative, plot

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.820
holes and poor editing.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.580
Audiences took note.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.160
In the end, The Hurricane Heist failed to
break $1 million on its first day and grossed

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:53.520
just over $6 million at the end of its theatrical
run, just one sixth of its production budget.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:55.300
Annihilation

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.260
Based on the critically-acclaimed Jeff VanderMeer
novel of the same name, Annihilation is the

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.960
story of a team of scientists who venture
into the Shimmer, a place unconfined by the

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.080
laws of reality.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.540
It’s also a very good movie, critics were
quick to sing its praises.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:15.160
Despite this, however, audiences responded
to its release with near-total indifference.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:16.740
“How is that possible?

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.840
You must be able to tell me something."

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:24.040
Paramount may have shot down Annihilation’s
box office chances by striking a deal for

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:27.140
the movie’s international streaming rights
prior to release.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:33.060
It dropped on Netflix around the time of its
theatrical release in virtually every market

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:37.440
except North America and China, severely cutting
into its overseas profits.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.280
In the States, it went up against Black Panther.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:45.400
Unsurprisingly, Annihilation failed to break
even on its $40 million budget.

